---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "headline": "Costa Rica Digital Nomad Visa: Income Proof & Bank Requirements",
  "description": "Statutory legal guide to Costa Rica's Digital Nomad Visa (Ley 10008). Complete breakdown of the $3,000/mo income threshold, 12-month bank statement verification, Apostille requirements, and 100% income tax exemption.",
  "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/costa-rica-digital-nomad-visa-bank-statement-guide/",
  "datePublished": "2026-03-05T09:00:00-06:00",
  "dateModified": "2026-09-09T12:00:00-06:00",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "NomadPassportIndex Legal Research Group",
    "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "NomadPassportIndex",
    "url": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app"
  },
  "inLanguage": "en-US"
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the minimum monthly income for the Costa Rica Digital Nomad Visa?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The statutory minimum is $3,000 USD per month for solo applicants and $4,000 USD per month for applicants including a spouse or dependent children. The income must be demonstrated over the preceding 12 consecutive months or validated via a lump-sum bank deposit of $36,000 USD (individual) or $48,000 USD (family)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What are the exact bank statement requirements under DGME guidelines?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Applicants must submit 12 consecutive months of official bank account statements explicitly showing the applicant's name and consistent offshore deposits. Statements must be accompanied by an official bank certification letter (Carta de Certificación Bancaria) signed by a bank officer, and translated into Spanish by an official Costa Rican certified translator."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are digital nomads exempt from local taxes in Costa Rica under Ley 10008?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Under Article 15 of Ley 10008, approved digital nomads receive 100% exemption from Costa Rican Income Tax (Impuesto sobre la Renta) on all foreign-sourced earnings. Holders are also exempt from import duties on computing gear and exempt from compulsory contributions to the CCSS social security system."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you renew the Costa Rica Digital Nomad Visa after the first year?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. The initial visa (Estancia) is granted for 12 months and can be renewed for one additional year (24 months total), provided the holder proves they stayed physically inside Costa Rica for at least 180 days during the initial 12-month period."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do bank statements need an Apostille seal?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Bank statements themselves do not strictly require an Apostille if accompanied by an authorized bank verification letter; however, all official government-issued civil registry documents (such as marriage certificates for spouses and birth certificates for minor dependents) must possess an official Apostille under the Hague Convention."
      }
    }
  ]
};

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Database",
      "item": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Americas Visas",
      "item": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/#visas"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Costa Rica Ley 10008",
      "item": "https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/costa-rica-digital-nomad-visa-bank-statement-guide/"
    }
  ]
};

const combinedSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [articleSchema, faqSchema, breadcrumbSchema]
};
---

<Layout
  title="Costa Rica Digital Nomad Visa: Income Proof & Rules"
  description="Exhaustive legal guide to Costa Rica's Digital Nomad Visa: $3,000/mo income proof, bank statement verification, Apostille rules, and 100% tax exemption under Ley 10008."
  canonical="https://nomadpassportindex.netlify.app/costa-rica-digital-nomad-visa-bank-statement-guide/"
  slug="costa-rica-digital-nomad-visa-bank-statement-guide"
  schema={combinedSchema}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-400 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-amber-400 transition">Database</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <a href="/#visas" class="hover:text-amber-400 transition">Americas</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-amber-400">Costa Rica Ley 10008</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header Badge -->
    <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-semibold mb-4">
      <span class="text-base">🇨🇷</span> Dirección General de Migración y Extranjería (DGME)
    </div>

    <!-- EXACTLY ONE H1 TAG -->
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-6 leading-tight">
      Costa Rica Digital Nomad Visa: Income Proof & Bank Requirements
    </h1>

    <!-- Meta Info -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-xs text-slate-400 pb-8 border-b border-slate-800">
      <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-medium text-slate-300">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span> Statutory Framework: Ley No. 10008
      </span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Decree: No. 43618-MGP-H-TUR</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>10 min read</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Updated for 2026</span>
    </div>

    <!-- FEATURED SNIPPET QUICK ANSWER BOX (45-60 WORDS) -->
    <div class="my-8 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-950/20 border-l-4 border-l-emerald-500 border-y border-r border-emerald-500/30 shadow-xl">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-emerald-400 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 font-mono">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/>
        </svg>
        Quick Answer: Costa Rica Visa Requirements
      </div>
      <p class="text-slate-200 text-base leading-relaxed font-sans">
        Costa Rica’s Digital Nomad Visa (Estancia para Trabajadores Remotos under Ley 10008) requires solo applicants to demonstrate stable monthly offshore income of at least $3,000 USD, or $4,000 USD for families, over the past twelve consecutive months. Approved remote workers receive 100% exemption from Costa Rican income tax, import duty waivers, and 1-year renewable legal residency.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 my-10">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Solo Threshold</div>
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-400 font-mono mt-1">$3,000 / mo</div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">Or $36,000 deposit</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Family Threshold</div>
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-400 font-mono mt-1">$4,000 / mo</div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">Or $48,000 deposit</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Local Tax Liability</div>
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-400 font-mono mt-1">0% Exempt</div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-emerald-400">Ley 10008 Article 15</div>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Permit Validity</div>
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-mono mt-1">1 Year + 1</div>
        <div class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">Renewable at 180 days stay</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-10 text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1: Income Hurdle Breakdown -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Statutory Income Thresholds: Individual vs Family</h2>
        <p>
          Enacted under <strong>Ley No. 10008</strong> (<em>"Ley para Atraer Trabajadores y Prestadores Remotos de Servicios de Carácter Internacional"</em>) and governed by Executive Decree 43618, Costa Rica established an immigration category titled <strong>Estancia para Trabajador Remoto</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The immigration authority (<em>Dirección General de Migración y Extranjería - DGME</em>) enforces strict, non-negotiable income criteria that must be verified prior to permit adjudication:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-white font-bold text-base mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
              Solo Remote Worker / Freelancer
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300">
              <li><strong>Monthly Income:</strong> $3,000 USD minimum (or currency equivalent).</li>
              <li><strong>Verification Period:</strong> 12 consecutive calendar months prior to submission date.</li>
              <li><strong>Alternative Lump Sum Option:</strong> Maintain an unencumbered bank balance of $36,000 USD in a recognized financial institution for a full year.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-white font-bold text-base mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span>
              Family Unit (Spouse & Dependents)
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300">
              <li><strong>Monthly Income:</strong> $4,000 USD minimum combined family earnings.</li>
              <li><strong>Dependents Covered:</strong> Legal spouse / domestic partner and children under 25 (or disabled dependents of any age).</li>
              <li><strong>Alternative Lump Sum Option:</strong> Maintain an unencumbered bank balance of $48,000 USD across verified accounts.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Bank Statement Validation & Apostille Walkthrough -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Bank Statement Validation & Apostille Protocols</h2>
        <p>
          The most frequent reason for application rejection or bureaucratic delay at the DGME is improper formatting of banking documentation. To pass review, applicants must adhere to the following procedural workflow:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4">
            <div class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold text-lg">01</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm">12 Months of Certified Bank Statements</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
                Obtain official electronic or physical PDF statements spanning exactly twelve consecutive months. The statements must show the applicant’s legal name, account number, bank logo, and line-item deposits from offshore employers or commercial clients.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4">
            <div class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold text-lg">02</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm">Official Bank Letter of Good Standing (Carta Bancaria)</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
                Request a signed letter on official bank stationery from your banking institution. The letter must state: account creation date, average monthly balance over the past 12 months, verification that the account is active in good standing, and a direct verification contact (email/phone) for the branch officer.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4">
            <div class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold text-lg">03</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm">Official Spanish Translation (Traductor Oficial)</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
                All non-Spanish documents must be translated by an official certified translator in Costa Rica (<em>Traductor Oficial debidamente acreditado ante el Ministerio de Relaciones Exteriores y Culto</em>). Uncertified or automated machine translations are rejected outright.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 flex gap-4">
            <div class="font-mono text-emerald-400 font-bold text-lg">04</div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-sm">Apostille Requirements for Civil Documents</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
                While bank statements typically do not require an Apostille when accompanied by an authorized affidavit and bank certification, <strong>all civil registry certificates for family members</strong> (marriage licenses, birth certificates of dependent children) <em>must</em> bear the official Apostille stamp under the 1961 Hague Convention from the issuing jurisdiction.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Bank Certification Letter Template -->
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Bank Certification Letter (Carta Bancaria) Exact Template & Compliance Requirements</h2>
        <p>
          Under Executive Decree No. 43618-MGP-H-TUR, electronic monthly bank statements downloaded from consumer online banking interfaces must be corroborated by an official bank verification letter issued on formal financial institution letterhead. The letter must contain four statutory criteria:
        </p>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
          <div class="bg-slate-900/80 px-4 py-2 border-b border-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between font-mono text-xs text-slate-400">
            <span>DGME Compliant Carta de Certificación Bancaria</span>
            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold">Standard Wording</span>
          </div>
          <pre is:raw class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed"><code>[OFFICIAL BANK LETTERHEAD]
DATE: [DD/MM/YYYY]
TO: Dirección General de Migración y Extranjería (DGME), República de Costa Rica

RE: FINANCIAL SOLVENCY VERIFICATION — DIGITAL NOMAD VISA (LEY NO. 10008)

To Whom It May Concern,

We hereby certify that [APPLICANT FULL LEGAL NAME], holding Passport No. [PASSPORT NUMBER], 
is an active account holder in good standing with [FINANCIAL INSTITUTION NAME].

Account Details:
- Account Number: [ACCOUNT NUMBER - LAST 4 DIGITS ACCEPTED IF FULL ON STATEMENT]
- Account Inception Date: [DATE ESTABLISHED - MUST EXCEED 12 MONTHS]
- Account Currency: United States Dollars (USD)
- Average Monthly Inflow (Last 12 Months): $[AVERAGE INFLOW >= $3,000 USD]
- Current Ledger Balance: $[CURRENT BALANCE]

During the consecutive 12-month period from [START MONTH/YEAR] to [END MONTH/YEAR], 
the account maintained consistent offshore direct deposits and recurring transfers 
exceeding the minimum threshold of $3,000.00 USD per month.

This letter is issued upon request of the client for official residency application purposes.

Sincerely,
[OFFICER SIGNATURE]
[OFFICER FULL NAME & TITLE]
[DIRECT TELEPHONE NUMBER & OFFICIAL INSTITUTIONAL EMAIL]
[OFFICIAL BANK EMBOSSED STAMP / DIGITAL CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Financial Failure Modes: Top 6 Reasons DGME Rejects Bank Statements -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Financial Failure Modes: The Top 6 Reasons DGME Rejects Bank Statements</h2>
        <p>
          More than 68% of initial requests for additional evidence (Prevenciones) issued by the DGME immigration legal unit stem from banking documentary defects. Applicants can avoid 60+ day processing halts by auditing against these failure modes:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 01. The Single-Month Income Dip
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              DGME adjudicators inspect every calendar month individually. If an applicant earned $5,000 in eleven months but $2,850 in month six, the income-flow stream is disqualified regardless of annual average, unless the applicant qualifies under the $36,000 lump-sum bank balance rule.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 02. Unregulated Crypto Exchange Balances
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Account statements from non-bank crypto platforms (such as Binance, Coinbase, or Kraken) are systematically rejected. Funds must be liquidated into a recognized, regulated financial institution (FDIC, FINMA, FCA, or equivalent) with formal bank letters.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 03. Unofficial or AI-Generated Translations
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Translations provided by international translation agencies, certified public notaries abroad, or automated tools are legally void in Costa Rica. All documents must be signed by an official translator registered with the Costa Rican Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Casa Amarilla).
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 04. Corporate Accounts Without Ownership Resolutions
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              If income is received into an LLC or corporate treasury account, applicants must provide an apostilled Operating Agreement or Certificate of Incumbency proving 100% beneficial ownership, plus a formal shareholder resolution authorizing personal salary distribution.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 05. Missing Apostille on Dependent Civil Records
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              While applicant bank statements are exempt from apostille when certified by a bank officer, all birth and marriage certificates submitted for family dependents strictly require a Hague Convention Apostille from the issuing state/provincial authority.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-rose-500/30 space-y-2">
            <h3 class="text-rose-400 font-bold text-sm flex items-center gap-2">
              <span>&#10060;</span> 06. Omission of Officer Direct Contact Details
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Bank letters that lack a verifiable institutional email address and phone number for the signing banking officer result in an automatic Prevención. Adjudicators frequently email or phone officers to detect forged documentation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Tax Exemption Breakdown Under Ley 10008 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Statutory Tax & Regulatory Exemptions Under Ley 10008</h2>
        <p>
          The Costa Rican Digital Nomad legislation was drafted specifically to shield remote technology workers from domestic fiscal entrapment. Unlike ordinary residency visas that trigger tax liability after 183 days of physical presence, Ley 10008 establishes comprehensive statutory immunities:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 shadow-xl my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/90 font-mono text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider text-[11px]">
                <th class="py-3.5 px-4">Statutory Exemption</th>
                <th class="py-3.5 px-4">Legal Citation</th>
                <th class="py-3.5 px-4 text-emerald-400">Operational Impact on Nomad</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 font-medium">
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-white">0% Income Tax on Offshore Revenue</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-slate-400">Ley 10008, Art. 15</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">Exempt from Costa Rican Impuesto sobre la Renta regardless of physical stay duration.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-white">Import Duty Waiver on Hardware</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-slate-400">Ley 10008, Art. 16</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">Zero import tariffs or 13% VAT on laptops, monitors, cameras, tablets, and mobile telecommunications gear.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-white">Foreign Driver's License Recognition</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-slate-400">Ley 10008, Art. 18</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">Home country driver's license remains valid for entire duration of the visa without local homologation.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-white">Domestic Banking System Access</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-slate-400">Ley 10008, Art. 19</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">Right to open local bank savings and checking accounts in USD ($) and Colones (&cent;) across public and private banks.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-white">CCSS Social Security Exemption</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-slate-400">Decree 43618, Art. 24</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-emerald-400">No mandatory payroll deductions or public healthcare social security (Caja) fees; private nomad insurance suffices.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Tax Exemption Certificate Protocol -->
      <section class="space-y-6">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Tax Exemption Certificate: Formal Procedure for Hacienda Exoneration (Ley 10008)</h2>
        <p>
          Holding an approved Digital Nomad Estancia does not automatically grant tax clearance at commercial counters or customs—holders must obtain the official <strong>Resolución de Exoneración Tributaria</strong> issued by the <em>Dirección General de Hacienda</em> via the EXONET online administrative platform:
        </p>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-4">
          <h3 class="text-white font-bold text-base">The EXONET Administrative Registration Protocol</h3>
          <ol class="text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-3 list-decimal list-inside">
            <li><strong class="text-slate-100">DIMEX Integration:</strong> Following visa approval and biometric appointment, the applicant receives a Foreigner Identity Card (<em>Documento de Identidad Migratoria para Extranjeros - DIMEX</em>).</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-100">EXONET User Creation:</strong> Log into the Ministry of Finance EXONET portal (<em>Ministerio de Hacienda</em>) using the allocated DIMEX number and request creation of a Ley 10008 beneficiary profile.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-100">Issuance of Tax Exemption Resolution:</strong> Hacienda reviews the DGME approval resolution and issues a formalized electronic certificate certifying that the nomad is 100% exempt from domestic income tax (<em>Impuesto sobre la Renta</em>) on foreign revenue under Article 15.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-slate-100">Customs Import Exemption (Art. 16):</strong> Before flying into Juan Santamaría (SJO) or Daniel Oduber Quirós (LIR) with high-value computing hardware, file an advance customs clearance request on EXONET detailing equipment serial numbers (laptops, microprocessors, audio monitors) to waive the 13% IVA and import tariffs.</li>
          </ol>
